# Voyager App Backend — Project Overview

- Repository root: [pyproject.toml](mdc:pyproject.toml)
- Source root: [src/](mdc:src)
- FastAPI app entry: [src/app/main.py](mdc:src/app/main.py)
- CLI entry: [src/app/cli.py](mdc:src/app/cli.py)
- Configuration loader: [src/app/config.py](mdc:src/app/config.py)
- Hydra config: [src/conf/config.yaml](mdc:src/conf/config.yaml), [src/conf/env/dev.yaml](mdc:src/conf/env/dev.yaml), [src/conf/env/prod.yaml](mdc:src/conf/env/prod.yaml)
- Path utilities: [src/utils/paths.py](mdc:src/utils/paths.py)
- Getting started: [README.md](mdc:README.md)

## Runtime

- Python 3.13+
- Package/runtime manager: uv (see [pyproject.toml](mdc:pyproject.toml))

## How to run

```bash
uv sync
uv run dev   # Fast refresh server with APP_ENV=dev
uv run prod  # Production server with APP_ENV=prod
```

## Entry points

- FastAPI app: [src/app/main.py](mdc:src/app/main.py)
  - Uses lifespan to load configuration once and attach it to `app.state.config`.
  - Emits a startup banner via the `uvicorn.error` logger at WARNING level showing only non-sensitive metadata.
- CLI wrappers: [src/app/cli.py](mdc:src/app/cli.py)
  - `dev()` runs `fastapi dev` with `APP_ENV=dev`.
  - `prod()` runs `fastapi run` with `APP_ENV=prod`.

## Configuration

- Loader: [src/app/config.py](mdc:src/app/config.py)
  - `.env` is loaded via `dotenv` (override=False).
  - Hydra composes from [src/conf/](mdc:src/conf) with defaults to `env=dev` unless `APP_ENV` is provided.
  - The selected environment name is exposed at `cfg.app.env`.
